# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-safe-recoveries.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/398-stop-execute-file-allowlist/requirements.md

Feature: Stop execute File(s) allowlisting
  Execute workers satisfy Approved outcomes while immutable inputs and unsafe
  publication paths remain denied.

  @AC1 @SCN001
  Scenario: Missing File(s) does not block implement preflight
    Given a singular Approved spec whose tasks omit File(s)
    When execute inspects publication scope before implement dispatch
    Then inspection succeeds with mutationPolicy outcome
    And it does not report publication_scope_unproven
    And all four current spec inputs are read-only

  @AC2 @SCN002
  Scenario: PathCast-shaped fix publishes extra required paths
    Given an Approved task names only one product file in File(s)
    And fix1 dirties additional mobile/test/features/step files
    And fix1 dirties the current specs/398-stop-execute-file-allowlist/verification-report.md
    When apply-review publishes with --applied
    Then it commits every observed dirty path with the review-fix subject
    And it does not emit Review fixes exceed approved task scope

  @AC3 @SCN003
  Scenario: Dirty Approved spec input fails closed
    Given apply-review dirties specs/398-stop-execute-file-allowlist/tasks.md
    When it inspects observed publication paths
    Then publication fails closed naming that denied path
    And no commit or push occurs

  @AC4 @SCN004
  Scenario: Parsed File(s) remain optional hints
    Given an Approved task lists a subset of required product paths
    When implement, fix1, and fix2 publication scope is inspected
    Then each scope reports mutationPolicy outcome
    And allowedPaths contains only parsed hints rather than a mutation ceiling
    And readOnlyPaths contains requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md, and feature.gherkin

  @AC5 @SCN005
  Scenario: Reconciliation proves the observed commit set
    Given a fix stage observes valid product and current verification-report paths
    When it commits and reconciles those paths
    Then every commit path is valid and non-denied
    And evidence allowedPaths equals the observed commit path set
    But verify remains closed to the current verification report
    And deliver retains its explicit artifact lists

  @AC6 @SCN006
  Scenario: Worker contracts authorize outcomes instead of task paths
    Given write-code receives a passing outcome-policy probe
    When Acceptance requires a valid path omitted from File(s)
    Then write-code may mutate and publish that non-denied path
    And it never edits a readOnlyPaths entry
    And write-spec treats canonical File(s) declarations as optional hints
